library: the C33 on Linux (musl)

std's per-architecture lists gain the C33: the generic stat layout of
riscv32, exception data in %r4/%r5, malloc's 8-byte minimum alignment.
There is no MMU, so no guard page for the stack-overflow handler to
fault on; the C33 takes handler_none.  The unwinder is libgcc's, as the
toolchain's C++ uses (gcc_eh static, gcc_s shared), and
_Unwind_Exception is aligned to GCC's BIGGEST_ALIGNMENT, 4.  libc comes
from ../../libc, the crate with the C33 added (patches/libc-0001).

